# x in the reader ticks a task the way the Tasks plugin does (tests/drive.rs reads the note
# back). Nothing read yet: the first task on screen. The note is shorter than the pane, so j
# moves the highlighted line down to the recurring task, whose next occurrence is added above.
# COLD_LAVA_TODAY pins the done date.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for example-workspace
keys p
type 2026-11-05
wait-for 1 note
keys enter
wait-for Journal/2026-11-05  reading
keys x
wait-for done: Write a note on lahars (Lahar is still unresolved)
wait-for ☑ Write a note on lahars
keys x
wait-for open again: Write a note on lahars
wait-for ☐ Write a note on lahars
keys j j j j j j j j j j x
wait-for done: Review the eruption timeline board · next occurrence added
wait-for ☑ Review the eruption timeline board
screen
keys esc
wait-gone reading · Esc / q back
keys q
exits 0
